  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID Promoting Rights and Justice in The Gambia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Gambia, The):  FY 2024 funds will support the USAID Promoting Rights and Justice activity in The Gambia to protect and promote the advancement of civic and political rights of Gambian citizens and civic entities. The purpose of this activity is to advance citizen knowledge of, use of, and ability to shape the law to exercise their civil and political rights safely, and improve the functionality of the justice system to protect the rights of all Gambians..Interventions under this activity are designed to improve institutions&apos; capabilities in the justice sector, including state and non-state entities, and complement the work of the Truth, Reconciliation, and Reparations Commission and the Janneh Commission. Results will include increased functionality and accountability of the justice sector. .The interventions will also support strengthening civil society and media organizations through organizational and financial capacity development, training programs, institutional network building, and activity-based support linked to rights and justice objectives. Activities will include training, coaching and mentoring, policy reform, the reform of administrative systems and processes, public outreach, advocacy, and capacity strengthening. .USAID will reinforce and enhance contributions by other donor partners, including the US State Department, the European Union, the United Kingdom, and United Nations agencies. ...</narrative>
  </description>
